WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.390
Yes, Indiana Jones is among the most beloved
of film franchises, but that doesn't mean

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:06.960
the movies are without their flaws.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.120
We've all rolled our eyes at the scene where
Indy survives a nuclear bomb by hiding in

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.999
a refrigerator, but here's a rundown of some
of the other less obvious but still pretty

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.840
dumb things that the Indiana Jones movies
ask its viewers to ignore.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.020
When Raiders of the Lost Ark opens, Indiana
Jones is unfazed by his colleague's stories

00:00:24.029 --> 00:00:28.770
about ancient, mystical powers that could
destroy everyone seeking the Ark of the Covenant.

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.880
By the end of the movie, once he's experienced
a bunch of ghosts with the power to melt Nazis'

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.520
faces off, he's forced to accept that there
are powers in the world well beyond his understanding.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.320
He even ends the movie by warning the government
agents that they don't know what they're dealing

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:41.820
with.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.040
"You don't look very happy."

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:44.880
"Fools.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.440
Bureaucratic fools."

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:46.940
"What'd they say?"

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.460
"They don't know what they've got there."

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.200
Great character arc, right?

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:55.360
Here's the problem: while it came out three
years after Raiders, Temple of Doom is actually

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.460
a prequel that takes place a year earlier.

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.360
In that movie, Indy saw a man's heart magically
ripped from his chest while still beating

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:06.240
and personally turned magic stones white-hot
by invoking the name of Shiva.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:10.380
Despite bearing witness to all that, Indiana
Jones is still a skeptic.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:14.360
In The Last Crusade, he's very quick to dismiss
stories about King Arthur and the Holy Grail

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:16.100
as "bedtime stories."

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.300
He's even still hanging onto those doubts
when Crystal Skull rolls around.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.670
It's one thing to try and ensure your character
can be relatable and realistic when he's dealing

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:28.500
with ancient, fantastical mysteries, but for
Indy to simply ignore some of the most exciting,

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.440
perplexing, and incredibly real moments of
his life is just silly.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:37.480
After thrilling chases, a couple of failed
rescue attempts, and outsmarting the bad guys

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:42.030
at every turn throughout Raiders of the Lost
Ark, Indiana Jones and Marion Ravenwood are

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:45.990
captured and forced to witness the hellish
moment when the bad guys open the Ark.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:49.520
As the power of the Ark is unleashed Indy
tells Marion that they can't look at it, no

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.780
matter what happens.

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:55.640
He's right, too: in the midst of a cadre of
Nazis being burned alive by the Wrath of God,

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:57.660
the good guys are spared from its wrath.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:00.280
So how in the world did Indy know not to look
at the ark?

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:04.400
Earlier in the film, it's mentioned that the
Ark was hidden away due to its immense power

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.229
being too much for mankind to handle, but
the cheat code of just closing one's eyes

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:09.799
came kind of out of nowhere.

00:02:09.799 --> 00:02:13.810
Also, we're not complaining, but it does seem
a little weird that nobody else figured out

00:02:13.810 --> 00:02:16.520
that they shouldn't look at the blinding light
that was melting everyone.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:20.780
As it turns out, Indy was warned about this
in a scene that was cut from the final version

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:21.560
of the movie.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:24.840
That might be a good way for Indy to know,
but the audience sure doesn't.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:29.020
It might seem like we're picking on Raiders,
but in a movie that's otherwise perfect, the

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.300
few flaws are really easy to spot.

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:33.860
Take, for instance, Indy's trip on a Nazi
sumbarine.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.300
The key word there is "on", not "in."

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:41.300
With the help of a friendly sea captain, Indy
stealths his way onto a U-Boat to rescue Marion

00:02:41.319 --> 00:02:44.810
and defeat Belloq, jumping atop it just before
it goes underwater.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.680
The film then cuts to an island where the
villains plan to open the Ark of the Covenant.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.500
So how did our soaking wet Indy survive the
trip?

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:55.659
Obviously, he couldn't just cling to the periscope
and hold his breath for hundreds of miles,

00:02:55.659 --> 00:02:59.720
but from what we see in the movie, and even
a deleted scene, that's exactly what happened.

00:02:59.720 --> 00:03:03.870
It's just a good thing nobody ever bothered
to lower the periscope for the entire trip,

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:08.040
or else we'd have to deal with the explanation
that Indy was secretly the lost king of Atlantis

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:08.820
all this time.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:13.840
When Temple of Doom opens, Indiana Jones is
accompanied by a young child named Wan Li,

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.810
who Jones refers to as Short Round.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:20.120
It's later revealed that the young Chinese
boy from Shanghai got busted trying to pick

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:23.170
the archeologist's pocket and they eventually
became friends.

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:24.160
"You make me poor!

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:25.460
No fun!"

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.900
While opinions are split about Short Round,
it's undeniable that he provided some comic

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:34.290
relief, and drove the getaway car, pulled
stunts as daring as his mentor, and even broke

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.579
Indy from a magic mind control trance.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.820
By the end of the film, they both return to
the small Indian village as triumphant heroes.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.240
After that...who knows?

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:45.260
The third movie opens with absolutely no mention
of Short Round.

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:49.120
There's not even a whisper of him, nor is
he mentioned in Raiders of the Lost Ark, which

00:03:49.129 --> 00:03:51.180
came after Temple of Doom chronologically.

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.430
Short Round is just gone after the credits
roll.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:57.609
Romantic partners like Willie come and go
for a rugged and handsome bachelor like Jones.

00:03:57.609 --> 00:04:01.049
The young child that he took under his wing
and brought thousands of miles from his home

00:04:01.049 --> 00:04:02.940
on numerous death-defying adventures?

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.800
You'd think they'd at least stay in touch.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:08.560
We might even be willing to forgive some of
Crystal Skull's more egregious sins if Indy's

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.980
successor turned out to be Ke Huy Quan instead
of Shia LaBeouf.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:17.160
There's...a lot to be upset about in Kingdom
of the Crystal Skull, but the most important

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.280
might just be that it shifts the genre of
the franchise in a way that just doesn't work.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:24.699
There's nothing wrong with a good science
fiction story, if that's what you want to

00:04:24.699 --> 00:04:28.760
call this movie, but for it to come in the
fourth installment of a franchise rooted in

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:34.230
pulpy, fantastical adventure after a nearly
20-year gap just feels jarring and unnecessary.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.740
"I've got a bad feeling about this."

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:42.680
The movie ends with Jones and his cohorts
finding a collection of alien skeletons with

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.460
one missing head.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.840
After returning the infamous crystal skull,
the aliens come to life and vacate Earth in

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:48.860
a flying saucer.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:53.160
Indiana Jones is a guy who frequently comes
across the unknown in his pursuits of ancient

00:04:53.169 --> 00:04:57.690
and mysterious artifacts, but Roswell aliens
are a very different kind of mysterious, even

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:02.620
if, and especially if, they show up 20 years
after he was dealing with Biblical goblets.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:06.639
They feel out of place in Indy's world of
historical legends and supernatural treasures.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:10.260
In short, never switch your genre in the fourth
movie of a series.

